Read and answer Google reviews from inside Paperclip

Adds the Reviews page to the gbp-reviews plugin so a person can reply to a Google review from Paperclip through the same guarded path the agent tool uses. The dashboard's location cards now open that location's reviews (newest first, unreplied on top, with 'Not replied yet' or 'Replied from Paperclip / by an agent / in Google'), a 'Last synced' line and a 'Sync now' button offered only from the location's own company. A location card with no reviews yet says so in a neutral colour instead of claiming everything is replied, and one with no rating yet says that instead of showing an empty star line. Opening a review shows it on the right with the reply Google holds right now, the 'Posts as: <location>, using the Google account <email>' line computed by the worker from settings and not editable, a text box whose unsent draft lives only in the browser (localStorage, every access wrapped in try/catch, cleared on a successful post), a 'Start from the suggested reply' button, and a character count against Google's 4096 limit. 'Post to Google' opens an inline confirm panel (not a modal) with the exact text, the same Posts-as line, the sentence that the reply is public and cannot be taken down by Paperclip, an 'I understand this will be public' tick and, when a reply is already on Google, the old and new text side by side plus a second 'Replace the reply that is already on Google' tick; the button ('Yes, post it' or 'Replace the reply on Google') is disabled until both hold and while posting. The panel mints one idempotency key when it opens and keeps it across a retry, minting a new one only when the text changes, so a double click or a lost connection cannot post twice. On success the draft is cleared, the detail, list and dashboard counts refresh, a host toast says 'Reply posted', or 'Already posted' with 'Google already had this reply; nothing was sent twice.' when the guard found the reply was already there, and a receipt lists the steps (checked Google, posted at time as location using account, recorded in Paperclip or 'not yet, the dashboard will catch up at the next sync', task still open with a link). The Post button is not rendered at all when posting is switched off, the view is HQ's roll-up, the location's Google account is not in the plugin settings at all, the account is there but not allowed for this company, Google could not be checked, an earlier attempt is pending, or the person's role can only read; one plain sentence takes its place, and a missing account gets its own sentence naming the key to look for rather than sending the reader hunting for an allow-list entry that cannot exist. The review, suggested reply and text box stay for copying into Google's console. All of that decision logic is a pure reducer (editorState.ts) tested under node, and one mapper (replyErrors.ts) turns bridge codes, the worker's [ECODE] sentences and the host's role refusals into plain sentences, never '[object Object]'. The view state is mirrored into ?location=&review= with popstate handling, the way phone-tools does. The allowReplies setting now says it covers people as well as agents; 'AI-drafted' becomes 'suggested' in the manifest, package.json and README; the README gains the 0.1.10 entry, the corrected note that email-sourced reviews open an issue but are not stored until the next sync, the new error codes, and a plain statement that the attended live post is still to be run. Version 0.1.10 in package.json and the manifest. package.json also gains pg and @types/pg as development-only dependencies, with the lock file to match, for one new test file that runs the reply-posts store against a real Postgres: it checks the rules that only the database can enforce (a posted key answers duplicate, a failed key restarts, a second key is refused while one is posting, and the review and company predicates hold), and it skips itself with a printed reason when GBP_REVIEWS_TEST_DATABASE_URL is not set. 31 new tests plus that one, so 164 in the plugin: 163 passing and the Postgres one skipped here because no connection string is set. Typecheck and build clean.

